INT. VELODROME INFIELD - EVENING

The wooden bowl rises steeply on every side. A string of fluorescent tubes buzzes overhead. In the infield, three women huddle by a rack of carbon bikes.

MAUREEN "MO" DALY, 50s, stopwatch lanyard, windbreaker faded to pink, stands with a whistle between her teeth. TAMSIN ROYCE, 20s, long braid, helmet buckled tight, grips a bike by the saddle. YUKI MORIMOTO, 20s, shorter, quicker, shakes out her legs one at a time.

MO
(to everyone)
Listen up. Relay swap is at the red line. Not before it, not after. At the line.

Tamsin nods. Yuki doesn't.

MO (CONT'D)
(to Yuki)
You hear me, Morimoto?

YUKI
I hear you.

MO
Then say it.

YUKI
Red line.

Mo pulls the whistle out. She turns to the stopwatch and mutters at it.

MO
(to herself)
Please, please just once, don't lie to me.

The whistle blows. Tamsin swings a leg over and pushes off, wheels humming on the boards. Yuki clips in and rolls to the start of the swap zone.

TAMSIN
(shouting as she passes)
Ready!

YUKI
Go!

Tamsin sprints a full lap, the bowl a blur behind her. Yuki pedals up the banking, eyes on her partner's back wheel. Mo clicks the watch, murmuring.

MO
(to herself)
Come on, come on.

The swap. Tamsin's hand lands on Yuki's hip and shoves. Yuki surges. For three pedal strokes everything is perfect.

Then Tamsin's rear wheel clips Yuki's front. A shriek of carbon. The bikes tangle and both riders go down, sliding along the boards in a spray of splinters.

MO (CONT'D)
(to everyone, a roar)
Stop! Everybody stop!

Silence except for a wheel spinning. Tamsin sits up first, rubbing her hip. Yuki lifts her head, helmet scuffed.

YUKI
(laughing)
I swapped on the line.

TAMSIN
You swapped on my foot.

MO
(to Yuki)
You okay?

YUKI
She hit me.

MO
(to Tamsin)
You?

TAMSIN
Fine. Mostly.

Mo lets out a breath and sits on the boards. She stares at the stopwatch.

MO
(to herself)
Best time of the season. Unbelievable.
